How to Be a Great Voice Over Artist (No Experience Needed)

In this step-by-step guide, you’ll learn how to become a successful voice over artist from scratch — no acting degree, no fancy studio, and no need to move to Los Angeles or New York City.

🎙 Inside this video:

• What voice acting is (and isn’t)
• The most in-demand types of voiceover work: commercials, audiobooks, eLearning, narration, animation, and video games
• How to train your voice using the 3 C’s — control, clarity, and connection
• The affordable beginner gear you actually need (no $2,000 mic required)
• How to set up a simple home studio
• Performance tips to sound natural, real, and hire-worthy
• Where to find paid voiceover jobs (freelance platforms, pay-to-play casting sites, and direct marketing)
• The mindset that separates successful voice actors from the rest

💼 Plus, get details on our upcoming Tom Parks Audiobook Masterclass — where you’ll learn how to build and grow your audiobook business from a pro who’s recorded over 800 titles (including Rich Dad Poor Dad).

